  "question": {
    "text": "Suppose the solution of the differential equation $\\frac{d y}{d x}=\\frac{(2+\\alpha) x-\\beta y+2}{\\beta x-2 \\alpha y-(\\beta \\gamma-4 \\alpha)}$ represents a circle passing through origin. Then the radius of this circle is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "O5346",
      "text": "2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Hnpps",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{17}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "stwOI",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9lUjx",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{d y}{d x}=\\frac{(2+\\alpha) x-\\beta y+2}{\\beta x-y(2 \\alpha+\\beta)+4 \\alpha} \\\\ & \\beta x d y-(2 \\alpha+\\beta) y d y+4 \\alpha d y=(2+\\alpha) x d x-\\beta y d x+2 d x \\\\ & \\beta(x d y+y d x)-(2 \\alpha+\\beta) y d y+4 \\alpha d y=(2+\\alpha) x d x+2 d x \\\\ & \\beta x y-\\frac{(2 \\alpha+\\beta) y^2}{2}+4 \\alpha y=\\frac{(2+\\alpha) x^2}{2}\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow \\beta=0 \\text { for this to be circle } \\\\ & (2+\\alpha) \\frac{x^2}{2}+\\alpha y^2+2 x-4 \\alpha y=0\\end{aligned}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/2tCuNAoqC1uSz-Blo6hWIKGyIKzWPqjaPL_VvjbXIG8.original.fullsize.png\"><br />$\\begin{aligned} & \\text { i.e. } 2 x^2+2 y^2+2 x-8 y=0 \\\\ & x^2+y^2+x-4 y=0 \\\\ & r d=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}+4}=\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{2}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
